# File Created: 07/08/05
# Location: Northern Arizona University
# Course: Qauntitative Reasoning

DOCUMENT();

loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'PGML.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');

$index = random(0, 2);
$loc   = ('An airline', 'A bus station', 'A train station')[$index];
$type  = ('flight',     'bus',           'train')[$index];

$num  = $index == 1 ? random(10,40) : random(25, 150);
$line = Compute(random(100, 250) . "x + " . random(100, 250))->reduce;

BEGIN_PGML

[$loc] has determined that the relationship between the number of passengers on a 
[$type] and the total weight of luggage stored in the baggage compartment can be
estimated by the least squares regression equation [` y = [$line] `]. 
Predict the weight of luggage for a [$type] with [$num] passengers.

Answer: [_]{$line->eval(x => $num)}{20} pounds

END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
This is found by substituting [`x= [$num]`] into the line [`y=[$line]`] or [` [$line->eval(x => $num)]`] pounds.
END_PGML_SOLUTION

ENDDOCUMENT();      